   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\">Hi,</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"> we are investigating a deer population in an area of interest<span> </span><b>A</b>, and the goal is to estimate the population density within<span> this area</span>. We thus systematically covered<span> </span><b>A</b><span> </span>with camera traps, and we concentrate on individuals which can be identified by individual patterns (such as antlers) and thus can apply SECR. The home rages of these animals are relatively large relative to the camera trap density and to the extend of<b><span> </span>A. </b>Furthermore, the area surrounding<b><span> </span>A</b><span> </span>is also used by deers, i.e., there are several home range centres outside<span> </span><b>A </b><span><span>with home-ranges partially overlapping with <b>A</b></span></span><b><span> </span></b>(see attached scheme). </div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\">After reading carefully the Efford &amp; Fewster paper in Oikos (2013)  (especially Figure 1) as well as the literature related to the SECR-package I am still not sure which approach is appropriate:</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\">(1) We could ignore the shape of<span> </span><b>A<span> </span></b>at the beginning but define the area of integration by a relatively wide buffer (respectively buffer width as estimated from the data) leading to a larger area<span> </span><b>B<span> </span></b>comprising<b><span> </span>A</b>. This gives us an unbiased estimate of the number of animals with home ranges overlapping with at least one camera trap (red circles in the attached scheme). However, the animal density with respect to <b>B<span> </span></b>should be<b> </b>underestimated here, since there are several home ranges not overlapping with a camera but with the outer regions of <b>B<span> </span></b>(see attached scheme). Thus, we can&#39;t adopt this density for<b><span> </span>A </b><span>as far as I see.<br></span><b></b></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\">(2)  Instead we could force secr.fit() to restrict the area of interest to  <b>A</b>. However,  as far as I understand also these results would be biased, since some caught animals would have home-range centres outside<b> A</b>, but home ranges are forced to lie within <b>A.</b></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><b><br></b></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><span>I would be very happy if somebody has an idea how to solve this. </span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><span><br></span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><span>Thank you very much in advance,</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><span><br></span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><span>Moritz</span></div><br></div>"
